From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configs: orangepi_zero2: know the SPI NOR chips fitted to the board

The Zero2 has a 2 MiB SPI NOR (XT25F16B on most boards, Macronix on
others) that U-Boot's SPL can boot from (CONFIG_SPL_SPI_SUNXI). The SPL
reads the flash with raw commands, but U-Boot proper's `sf probe` needs
the JEDEC ID in its tables; only Macronix is enabled upstream. Add the
vendors seen on H616 boards so `sf probe` / `sf read` work for
inspection and recovery from the U-Boot prompt.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
+++ b/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
@@ -20,7 +20,14 @@
 CONFIG_SYS_I2C_SLAVE=0x7f
 CONFIG_SYS_I2C_SPEED=400000
 CONFIG_MTD=y
+CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_EON=y
+CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_GIGADEVICE=y
 CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_MACRONIX=y
+CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_PUYA=y
+CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_WINBOND=y
+CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_XMC=y
+CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_XTX=y
+CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_ZBIT=y
 CONFIG_SUN8I_EMAC=y
 CONFIG_PHY_REALTEK=y
 CONFIG_AXP305_POWER=y
